🔍 Detecting Race Conditions

Detection methods:

Analyze application states

Monitor transaction logs

Test concurrency behavior

Perform parallel request testing

Use tools like Burp Repeater

🛡 Mitigation Techniques
1️⃣ Synchronization Locks

Only one thread can access resource at a time.

Example:

mutex locks
2️⃣ Atomic Operations

Operations executed as a single indivisible step.

Example:

balance -= amount
3️⃣ Database Transactions

Ensures operations complete together.

BEGIN TRANSACTION
UPDATE balance
COMMIT

Prevents inconsistent data.

⚠ Real-World Impact

Race conditions have caused:

Cryptocurrency exchange exploits

Gift card abuse

Financial fraud

Payment bypass attacks

🎯 Key Takeaways

Race conditions exploit timing flaws.

Shared resources create vulnerabilities.

Multi-threaded systems increase risk.

Parallel requests can bypass logic checks.

Proper locking and transactions prevent exploitation.

